<title>CHINA: China Pingan pays $42,200 after mine disaster.</title>
<headline>China Pingan pays $42,200 after mine disaster.</headline>
<dateline>BEIJING 1997-06-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>A subsidiary of China's Pingan Insurance Co has paid 350,000 yuan ($42,200) in compensation after a mine disaster that killed 60 in northeastern Liaoning province, the Financial News said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The insurance company delivered a cheque for initial compensation to managers just two days after the gas explosion rocked the Beilongfeng mine in Liaoning's Fushun city on May 28, the newspaper said.</p>
<p>It gave no details of what the money would cover but said the Shenyang-based subsidiary of Shenzhen-based Pingan Insurance accelerated payment to help the families of the disaster victims.</p>
<p>($1.0 = 8.3 yuan)</p>
<p>-- Beijing newsroom (8610) 6532-1921</p>
</text>
